A||N||1||silverstreak||Changing Auto to 5 speed????||||5||
Z||000000||silverstreak||05-24-2001||10:06 PM||||I am wanting to change out my automatic transmission to a 5-speed.  How hard is it to add the pedals and the cabling??  Is this possible or a mechanical nightmare?  Both transmissions were on 4-cylinders, but I will upgrading to an LT-1.  Thanks ||||reg||5
Z||000001||danny boy||05-24-2001||10:25 PM|||| It's a straight forward swap. All the mounting holes are already there, just remove the blockoff plates. Make sure you get everything from the same car so you know you got it all. From what I've heard, the shifters,cables and slave cyl are different depending on what tranny is in the car. Make sure parts are from a 5sp car. Also you'kll need to change from a neutral safety switch to the manual version.<BR> list of stuff you'll need:<BR>shifter assy.<BR>cables<BR>clutch/brake pedal assy.<BR>mastre cyl<BR>slave cyl<BR>lines<BR>||||reg||1
